Breaks: the orphan scan checks its listing only against the metadata read before it, so a file committed during the listing is queued as an orphan.
Module: catalog-maintenance
Test: OrphanRaceTest#aFileCommittedBetweenTheListingAndTheSecondReadIsReachable
diff --git a/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/OrphanScan.java b/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/OrphanScan.java
index 947db92..042c40c 100644
--- a/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/OrphanScan.java
+++ b/catalog-maintenance/src/main/java/nuna/maintenance/OrphanScan.java
@@ -66,7 +66,6 @@ final class OrphanScan {
         table.refresh();
         Reach since = reach.next();
         since.collect(metadata(table), table.io());
-        candidates.removeIf(location -> since.files.contains(Storage.normalize(location)));
         return candidates;
     }
 
